# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js — every build directory, however it is named.
#
# `next build` writes its output to whatever `PHMG_DIST_DIR` says
# (next.config.mjs), so the builds that must not touch a running dev server
# land in .next-check, .next-build-check, .next-e2e and whatever the next
# one is called. Listing them one by one failed exactly once and cost a
# 400 MB webpack cache in a commit GitHub refused: the glob covers the
# directory nobody has thought of yet.
/.next*/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template, which has no secrets in it and must be in the repo
!.env.example
# ...and the browser suite's environment, whose every value is throwaway.
# Committed so CI can run the suite without a file somebody writes by hand.
# It holds no MONGODB_URI: scripts/e2e.mjs supplies a throwaway one.
!.env.test

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local env
.env*.local
.env

# the local gateway's config, vault and logs (docker-compose.gateway.yml).
# Holds the shared secret and the encryption key, and the vault holds real
# file bytes — none of it belongs in the repo. docs/GATEWAY_DEPLOY.md has the
# command that creates it.
/.gateway-local/

# test output
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# local file vault (development storage driver)
.storage/
# ...and the browser suite's own, from STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR in .env.test, so a
# test run's files never land beside a developer's
.storage-test/
.taste-skill/
